---
import DemoShell from '../DemoShell.astro';
import Control from './Control.astro';
---

<DemoShell
  id="demo-microstructure"
  code="D5"
  title="Microstructure & tortuosity"
  poster="d5-microstructure.png"
  alt="A stochastic packing of dark circular particles with the transport potential shown in colour through the pore space between them"
  aspect="8/5"
  caption="A random particle packing with the steady diffusion field solved through its pores. The effective diffusivity is measured from the computed flux and set against the two formulas people usually reach for."
  presets={[
    { label: 'Dense electrode: ε = 0.40, transport squeezes through necks', state: { 'd5-eps': 0.4 } },
    { label: 'Open structure: ε = 0.85', state: { 'd5-eps': 0.85 } },
    { label: 'Fine particles, same porosity', state: { 'd5-r': 4, 'd5-eps': 0.55 } },
  ]}
>
  <fieldset class="panel" slot="panel" disabled>
    <legend>microstructure generator</legend>
    <Control id="d5-eps" label="target porosity ε" min={0.35} max={0.9} value={0.55} step={0.01} />
    <Control id="d5-r" label="particle radius / px" min={4} max={14} value={8} step={1} />
    <Control id="d5-s" label="polydispersity / ±%" min={0} max={50} value={25} step={5} />
    <div class="switch-row">
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="d5-lines" checked /> streamlines</label>
      <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="d5-reseed">new packing</button>
    </div>
    <table class="readout-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th class="num">D_eff / D₀</th><th class="num">τ</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="is-measured">
          <th scope="row">measured</th>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-deff">—</output></td>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-tort">—</output></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">2D bound ε/(2−ε)</th>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-maxwell">—</output></td>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-tort-maxwell">—</output></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Bruggeman ε^1.5</th>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-brugg">—</output></td>
          <td class="num"><output id="d5-tort-brugg">—</output></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="panel-readouts">
      <span>ε achieved <output id="d5-meas-eps">—</output></span>
      <span id="d5-sat-note" hidden>RSA jamming limit: <output id="d5-sat">—</output></span>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <p>
      The packing is generated by random sequential adsorption: disks are dropped at random and
      rejected if they overlap. The steady Laplace field is then solved through the pore phase by
      conjugate gradient on a 5-point stencil, with each face weighted by how open it is. Particle
      boundaries are sampled eight times per axis rather than rounded to whole cells, which keeps
      the discretisation error under 2% (whole-cell rounding cost 28% at low porosity).
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>2D bound ε/(2−ε).</strong> The 2D result for insulating circular inclusions
        (equivalently (1−f)/(1+f) with f = 1−ε the solid fraction). It is an upper bound, so the
        measurement has to sit below it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bruggeman ε^1.5.</strong> A correlation for 3D spheres, shown because it is what
        practitioners reach for. Above ε ≈ 0.382 it exceeds what any 2D geometry can achieve, so
        comparing a 2D packing with it flatters neither.
      </li>
      <li>
        τ here is defined by D<sub>eff</sub>/D₀ = ε/τ, so each row's τ is its ε divided by its
        D<sub>eff</sub>/D₀.
      </li>
      <li>
        Rejecting overlaps crowds the disks towards tangency, so as porosity falls transport is
        throttled by the narrow necks between them. The same packing seed is kept while you move a
        slider; "new packing" draws another.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</DemoShell>

<script>
  import { initWhenVisible } from './runtime';
  initWhenVisible('demo-microstructure', async (shell) => {
    const { init } = await import('./d5-microstructure');
    init(shell);
  });
</script>
